We are building a high-performance ADAS Online team focused on advancing state-of-the-art machine learning and AI algorithms for scene understanding and environmental awareness.
As a machine learning applied scientist, you will contribute to the development and improvement of models within the in-vehicle spatial awareness stack. Work hands-on across data, experimentation, and evaluation pipelines, and grow your ability to tackle increasingly complex engineering challenges in a fast-moving team.
This spatial awareness stack will leverage modern transformer and end-to-end architectures to transform vehicle sensor data along with real-time 3D map data from the cloud into a 3D, semantically defined environment identifying all static and dynamic objects.
What You’ll Do
Develop a solid understanding of the team's physical AI roadmap and contribute ideas that improve algorithms within your area of ownership;
Implement and improve ML / vision transformer models for 3D awareness;
Produce instance detections and segmentation masks, instance tracking, and occupancy modelling;
Contribute to multi-modal fusion pipelines (camera, LiDAR, RADAR), building and validating components against defined requirements;
Apply Transformer-based and representation learning techniques within established frameworks, building confidence in large-scale model development;
